<title>GERMANY: Germany's data processors see further growth - IFO.</title>
<headline>Germany's data processors see further growth - IFO.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Companies in the German data processing industry expect growth in the sector to continue and are hiring new staff on that basis, a report by the German economic research institute IFO said on Sunday.</p>
<p>In the second quarter of 1996 employment in the sector increased by two percent, slightly lower than in the same quarter in 1995, and companies surveyed said that the recent surging growth in the industry had fallen off slightly.</p>
<p>A majority of the data processing companies surveyed by IFO, which account for 21.4 billion marks in turnover and make up around 80 percent of the German market for data processing services, described their current business situation as &quot;good&quot;.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
